From e8daab79e7366d3cad41c9075213c1a93f605869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:04:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 09/19] GFS_surface_composites_pre: keep the land snow with
 frac_grid

composites_post sets weasd = txl*weasd_lnd + txi*weasd_ice; composites_pre then
set weasd_lnd = weasd for every LSM but RUC. With frac_grid weasd_lnd is the
persistent land value (Sfcprop%weasdl, initialised at cold start by dividing
out the land and ice fractions), so coastal land snow was diluted every step.
Noah-MP rebuilds layered snow from its snow layers (which made its water
check, errwat, report +16 mm per land column per 6 h); thin snow was lost.

Skip the overwrite with frac_grid, as already done for RUC.

Measured with in-model meters (with the single-step fix): Noah-MP's errwat
falls from +5 kg/m2 per 6 h (global mean) to -6e-5, and nothing outside
Noah-MP changes land water any more.
---
 .../UFS_SCM_NEPTUNE/GFS_surface_composites_pre.F90             | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/physics/Interstitials/UFS_SCM_NEPTUNE/GFS_surface_composites_pre.F90 b/physics/Interstitials/UFS_SCM_NEPTUNE/GFS_surface_composites_pre.F90
index 4279e63c..084f8b1d 100644
--- a/physics/Interstitials/UFS_SCM_NEPTUNE/GFS_surface_composites_pre.F90
+++ b/physics/Interstitials/UFS_SCM_NEPTUNE/GFS_surface_composites_pre.F90
@@ -234,7 +234,8 @@ contains
         endif
         if (dry(i)) then                   ! Land
           uustar_lnd(i) = uustar(i)
-           if(lsm /= lsm_ruc) weasd_lnd(i) = weasd(i)
+           ! with frac_grid, weasd is the cell mean and weasd_lnd the persistent land value (Sfcprop%weasdl)
+           if(lsm /= lsm_ruc .and. .not. frac_grid) weasd_lnd(i) = weasd(i)
            tsurf_lnd(i) = tsfcl(i)
         ! DH*
         else
